.TH GHSTARS 1 "2026-08-26" "ghstars 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ghstars \- classify GitHub starred repositories with GitHub Lists
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghstars
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ghstars
is a terminal tool for managing GitHub starred repositories.
GitHub Lists are the source of truth for classification and membership.
The program stores a local snapshot under
.IR ~/.ghstars/state/ .
It stores user configuration under
.IR ~/.ghstars/config/ .
.PP
Run
.B ghstars sync
before commands that use the local snapshot.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Fetch Stars and Lists from GitHub.
Use
.B --json
for structured output.
Use
.B --debug
for fetch and pagination details.
.TP
.B stars
List locally synced Stars with filters, search, sorting, and paging.
Use
.B --json
for structured output.
Use
.BI --fields " names"
to select comma-separated fields.
Use
.B --details
for the detailed field set.
.TP
.B github-lists
List locally synced GitHub Lists with parsed Intent and Category values.
The command supports
.B --json ,
.B --details ,
and
.BR --fields .
.TP
.B facets
Show filter values from the local snapshot.
Use
.B --json
for structured output.
.TP
.B status
Report local counts and offline verification results.
The command never calls GitHub.
.TP
.B ratelimit
Report the live GitHub API rate limit.
This is the only network call made by this command and it never runs a sync.
.TP
.B retriage
List local edits that lost a GitHub membership conflict.
The command supports
.B --json
and
.BR --fields .
.TP
.BI tag " OWNER/REPO LIST"
Add a Star to a List and push the change to GitHub.
Use
.B --private
when ghstars must create a private List.
New Lists are public by default.
.TP
.BI unstar " OWNER/REPO"
Unstar one or more explicitly named repositories on GitHub and mark their
local records Archived.
This command changes the GitHub account.
.B --yes
is required for every target.
.TP
.B category rename
Rename one Category across its Explore, Current, and Retired Lists.
.TP
.B category drain
Move all Stars from one Category to another while retaining each Intent.
Use
.B --private
for new destination Lists.
.TP
.B export
Write configured exports from the local snapshot.
The command reads the
.B [export]
table in
.IR ~/.ghstars/config/ghstars.toml .
.TP
.B diff
Show changes through the user's Git history under
.IR state/ .
Use
.B --log
for patch history instead of the working-tree diff.
Extra arguments pass to Git.
.TP
.B tui
Open the interactive Textual interface.
See
.BR ghstars-tui (1).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B --install-completion
Install shell completion.
.TP
.B --show-completion
Print shell completion.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ghstars/config/tui.toml
TUI configuration.
See
.BR ghstars-tui (5).
.TP
.I ~/.ghstars/config/ghstars.toml
Core configuration, including the
.B [export]
table.
.TP
.I ~/.ghstars/state/
Local Star, List, Retriage Queue, and TUI state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GHSTARS_HOME
Override the default
.IR ~/.ghstars/
state and config directory.
.TP
.B GHSTARS_DEBUG=1
Enable sync debug output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit status 0 means success.
Exit status 1 means a terminal failure.
Exit status 2 means a Typer usage error.
Exit status 3 means a retryable failure.
Exit status 4 means a partial bulk failure.
The
.B diff
command returns Git's exit status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ghstars-tui (1),
.BR ghstars-tui (5),
.BR gh (1),
.BR git (1)
